_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled back `payments-worker` from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0 in all three production regions and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001), which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` is healthy again on v3.3.0, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open under `payments-worker`. The summary records the rollback and the denied `payments-api` action.\n- **Denied action:** I first tried to roll back `payments-api` to v5.0.0, the last healthy release, but a human reviewer denied it as the wrong service and said the problem is in `payments-worker`. I then checked `payments-worker` and found the same 0.18 error rate on v3.4.0, with v3.3.0 as its last healthy release, so I rolled it back.\n\n**`payments-api` is still degraded.** It is running v5.1.0 with an 0.18 error rate, and I did not change it. If v5.1.0 is also contributing to the payments errors, it still needs attention. The reviewer's denial doesn't rule that out, so you or the on-call engineer should check it.", "type": "text"}]}]}